From: brainux-pw-a9300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/tiny: brain-lq050j1ug01: prefer depth 16

The plane only takes RGB565, but the driver leaves preferred_depth at 0.
The Xorg modesetting driver then probes for 32 bpp: it creates a dumb
buffer of the minimum size and adds an XRGB8888 framebuffer, which is
refused. It falls back to 24 bpp, which the plane does not take either,
so setting the mode fails and X keeps retrying ("failed to add fb -22").
With DRM_CAP_DUMB_PREFERRED_DEPTH at 16, modesetting uses 16 bpp
directly.

Through modesetting, X tells the driver what changed and the frame goes
to the panel right away. Through the fbdev emulation (Xorg's fbdev
driver), deferred I/O sends it at most every 50 ms, so the pointer moved
20 times a second at most.

Seen on Brain PW-A9300 with Xorg 21.1.16 (Debian trixie).

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/brain-lq050j1ug01.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/brain-lq050j1ug01.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/brain-lq050j1ug01.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/brain-lq050j1ug01.c
@@ -678,6 +678,8 @@
 	drm->mode_config.max_width = width;
 	drm->mode_config.min_height = height;
 	drm->mode_config.max_height = height;
+	/* The plane only takes RGB565 (see formats). */
+	drm->mode_config.preferred_depth = 16;

 	drm_connector_helper_add(&ili->connector, &brain_connector_helper_funcs);
 	ret = drm_connector_init(drm, &ili->connector, &brain_connector_funcs, DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_DPI);
